cellPad: keyboard right stick and L3/R3; PAD_FILE can hold the sticks.

A first-person game cannot be played from the keyboard without a camera: the keyboard fallback left the right stick
centred and had no L3/R3. I/J/K/L now drive the right stick and C/V press L3/R3. (Resistance 3 is played with the
shooter layout of 0004; this one stays the pad-shaped default.)

PAD_FILE accepts four optional stick values after the report count ("mask reports lx ly rx ry", 0-255, 128 centred),
held for those reports, the last one included, so scripted runs can walk and turn.

Test: test_pad_keyboard (C/V and I/J/K/L through the fake SDL keyboard) and the `sticks` case of test_pad_file_reports
(tools/test_pad_file_reports.py): the sticks are held for the press's reports, clamped, and then released.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
